+# OpenClaw-maintained A2UI compatibility patch
+
+This is a locally rebuilt, modified derivative of **@a2ui/lit@0.11.0**. It is not an upstream A2UI release or an upstream-signed modified package. The unchanged upstream Apache-2.0 LICENSE remains in this package.
+
+- Upstream source repository: https://github.com/a2ui-project/a2ui (renderers/lit). The published npm metadata does not supply a gitHead; an upstream source commit is unavailable and is not inferred.
+- Official archive: https://registry.npmjs.org/@a2ui/lit/-/lit-0.11.0.tgz
+- Official archive SRI: `sha512-HIJbubc9wKr/3zG1k1tGmZuI4XaAQrBVj7z6BY1fswLL7Q+q/8lwkiR4Pif2mMX88WCPcV2HoriPUk+X0PHnCA==`
+- Official archive SHA256: `d1df6346013bef1a28e499ac0676691813ce526c30e72b2a825e717ea010691c`
+- Migration source diff SHA256: `190b6be99bc5deee417392a6eb57e95d61b67f1c71bb768c4641d1981bd89e65` (preserved separately as a2ui-0.11.0-zod4.6.6-source.patch).
+- OpenClaw consumer source used for local qualification: `6fe800b8ce1e579cbc0074e2fffca2bbc28afa1a`, tree `c90e644f2d033cc86b39f4d517374b70ec38bf0a`. This identifies the consumer, not the upstream A2UI source or a final integrated release.
+
+The migration targets Zod 4.6.6. web_core uses public Zod 4 schema/ref handling and a native JSON Schema conversion adapter; lit changes only its declared Zod dependency. Some inline catalog wire schemas intentionally expand former dangling local references. This is tested-path compatibility, not arbitrary Zod 3-to-4 schema equivalence.
+
+Changed JavaScript, declaration files, and maps were generated from the preserved migration TypeScript with TypeScript 7.1.0-dev.20260920.1. Map source identities/content are normalized to package-local TypeScript names. Unchanged upstream package files and public export paths remain intact. The dependency graph must be updated by the package manager's normal resolver; this package.json patch alone is not dependency-graph evidence.
+
+Remove this patch only after an upstream replacement supports these exact Zod 4 consumers and the installed/restored package, type, catalog/ref/default, JSONL, and real Canvas browser qualifications pass. No automatic expiry or deployment is implied.
